  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value fell 3.5% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $14.40B (3.5% lower over 30D) hints that tokenized asset growth paused or reversed\u2014more consistent with risk-off allocation or redemptions than a pure news cycle. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/malaysia-central-bank-tokenized-bonds-sukuk-dlt-platform?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Malaysia central bank launches DLT platform for tokenized bonds</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/defi/ondo-perps-adds-3x-openai-pre-ipo-contract\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ondo Perps Adds 3x OpenAI Pre-IPO Contract</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Institutional commitments are still a leading share signal:</strong> Bank and asset-manager distribution deals often shift platform and network leadership before headline RWA totals fully catch up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/10/22/bitcoin-slides-below-usd82-000-as-ai-doubts-return-with-defi-tokens-leading-declines\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bitcoin slides below $82,000 as AI doubts return, with DeFi tokens leading declines</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/chainlink-cardano-and-other-blockchain-groups-push-sec-for-clearer-crypto-rules?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chainlink, Cardano, other blockchain groups push SEC for clearer crypto rules</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
